# Retail Manager - Cursor Rules (.cursorrules)

# Architecture & Discipline Constraints
- Always search before writing code. Extend existing functions instead of duplicating.
- Delete obsolete code immediately in the same change.
- Never claim a task is completed without running real build tests:
  - Backend: `cd backend/local-bridge && npm run build`
  - Frontend: `cd frontend && npm run build`
  - Types: `npx tsc --noEmit`
- Multi-Branch Architecture:
  - `main-stihl-dibidani` (STIHL Dibidani Store)
  - `main-stihl-niamakoro` (STIHL Niamakoro Store)
  - `main-stores-dubai` (Dubai / Niamana Store)
  - `main-mpm-food` (MPM Food Restaurant)
- When fixing an error from Sentry or CI/CD, document the issue in `memory-bank/errors/ERRORS_<BRANCH>.md` including the Computer Role, Organization, Operating System, and Verification output.
